---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How it works"
  description="Storm architecture: Flutter clients, a Rust sync server, plain Markdown vaults, and MCP for AI agents."
>
  <header class="page-hero wrap-narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">03 · Architecture</p>
    <h1>One knowledge layer. Many interfaces.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Storm is intentionally small. This page is the sketch; depth lives in the
      repository.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section wrap-narrow">
    <h2>Shape</h2>
    <p class="support">
      Clients on macOS, Android, and web — one Flutter codebase — talk REST and a
      WebSocket to <strong>storm-server</strong>, a Rust binary you run.
      The server owns merge, search, tags, attachments, and version history.
      Notes remain plain Markdown under a storage root you control. Compatible
      AI agents reach the same vault through MCP.
    </p>
    <pre class="diagram" aria-label="Architecture sketch"><code>{`macOS · Android · Web
          │  REST + WebSocket
          ▼
   storm-server (Rust / axum)
          │
   ┌──────┴──────┐
   ▼             ▼
vaults/*.md   state/
plain md      indexes · registry · auth.db
                     ▲
                     │ MCP
              AI applications`}</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap-narrow">
    <h2>Invariants that matter</h2>
    <ul class="points">
      <li>
        <strong>The vault is plain Markdown.</strong> Storm state lives in a
        sibling <code>state/</code> directory, never mixed into notes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Notes are tracked by UUID,</strong> so renames and moves are
        metadata, not new identity.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The server owns the canonical vault.</strong> Clients cache and
        queue; a merged or conflict response means the client adopts the
        server’s text.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Conflicts stay in the file.</strong> When a merge cannot finish
        cleanly, markers are written into the note — not a hidden sibling copy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Offline is normal.</strong> Creates and edits queue on the
        device and replay when the server returns. Search remains server-side.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Accounts are local and yours.</strong> An owner account,
        per-device pairing, sessions, and revocable keys for MCP clients — all
        in <code>state/auth.db</code> on your server. No cloud account, no
        third-party identity provider, no credential that leaves the network you
        control. One person with several devices is the default, not the limit.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap-narrow">
    <h2>Go deeper</h2>
    <p class="support">
      Living plan and decisions:
      <a
        href="https://github.com/dewanshDT/Storm/blob/main/PLAN.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">PLAN.md</a
      >. Deploy and apt:
      <a
        href="https://github.com/dewanshDT/Storm/tree/main/deploy"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">deploy/</a
      >. Server and MCP:
      <a
        href="https://github.com/dewanshDT/Storm/blob/main/apps/server/README.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">apps/server/README.md</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/install">Install</a>
      <a
        class="btn btn-ghost"
        href="https://github.com/dewanshDT/Storm"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Repository</a
      >
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .diagram {
    margin: 0;
    padding: calc(var(--sp) * 2.5);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: var(--bw) solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--r-card);
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text2);
  }

  .diagram code {
    font: inherit;
    color: inherit;
  }

  .points {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: calc(var(--sp) * 3);
  }

  .points li {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text2);
  }

  .points strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .points code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .support code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: calc(var(--sp) * 1.5);
    margin: calc(var(--sp) * 4) 0 0;
  }
</style>
